# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The database is disposable by design: while the system is being tested the
# data in it is test data, and DATA_LAYER.md says to delete the file to reset.
# Committed, it grew to 2.2 MB, dirtied the tree on every local run and
# blocked a pull. The schema rebuilds empty on the next request.
#
# A pattern, not a filename: icontrace.db was excluded by name twice before
# and a differently-named throwaway (icon_trace.db, trace.db) slipped past
# it and got committed anyway each time. Any *.db, wherever it turns up, is
# a database this project can rebuild from schema_sqlite.sql - never one to
# commit.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Runtime logs
*.log

# Uploaded invoices and generated documents, kept beside the app
storage/

# Session key — persisted to disk so restarts don't invalidate sessions.
# Never commit this; it is equivalent to a password.
.icon_secret
